  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating FGM prevention and abandonment in Baringo County Kenya-Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of this intervention is to protect young girls and women from Female genital mutilation (FGM) through;
-	Advocating the duty bearers and political leaders for increased commitment to FGM abandonment through legal frameworks, policies enforcement  and monitoring,
-	Sensitizing the rights holders to advocate the government to monitor and implement FGM legal policies and legal framework,
-	Inclusion of youths and strengthening of the formal and informal community structures as change agents and ambassadors in the fight against FGM.
- Strengthening the capacity and the outreach of FPFK and FPFK local churches in the fight against FGM  

The main activities of the intervention include:
- Training of duty bearers and political leaders on FGM data collection and use on FGM programming,
- Engagement of civil society with policy makers for FGM abandonment
- Development of sub-county FGM monitoring tools, advocacy strategies and FGM memos.</narrative>
  </description>
